# Template-owned shared code

`lbx-rl-tasks-iso-template` is the source of truth for shared tooling. The mothership
repo (`lbx-rl-tasks-iso-mothership`) receives those paths via
`sync-shared-from-template.yml` and overwrites local edits on every sync.

## When you are editing mothership

Do **not** modify template-owned paths in mothership. Make the change in
`lbx-rl-tasks-iso-template` instead, merge it, then run or wait for the mothership
workflow **Sync shared code from template**.

Wholesale (always template-owned):

- `.claude/skills`, `.cursor/rules`, `.cursor/skills`
- `.env.example`, `AGENTS.md`, `README.md`
- `alignerr_plugin/pyproject.toml`, `alignerr_plugin/src`
- `base`, `grader`, `harness`, `project_guidelines`
- `taiga_runtime/rubric/pyproject.toml`, `taiga_runtime/rubric/src`

Overlay (blocked in mothership only when the same relative path exists in the template):

- `docs/` (e.g. `docs/AUTHORING.md` → template; `docs/INFRA.md` → mothership-only OK)
- `scripts/` (e.g. `scripts/sync_mount.sh` → template; `scripts/poll_taiga_runs.py` → mothership-only OK)

Canonical list: mothership `configs/template-shared-sync.yaml`. CI check name:
`template-owned-paths`.

## When you are editing the template

Shared-tooling changes belong here. After merge, mothership picks them up through
the sync workflow (schedule / `template_shared_sync` / manual dispatch).
